def layout(title,description,slug,body,structured='',keywords=''):
    canonical='__SITE_URL__'+slug
    page=f'''<!doctype html><html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"/><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"/><meta name="theme-color" content="#080e20"/><meta name="color-scheme" content="dark"/>
<title>{escape(title)}</title><meta name="description" content="{escape(description,quote=True)}"/><meta name="robots" content="index,follow,max-image-preview:large"/><link rel="canonical" href="{canonical}"/>
<meta property="og:type" content="website"/><meta property="og:site_name" content="ORBIT"/><meta property="og:title" content="{escape(title,quote=True)}"/><meta property="og:description" content="{escape(description,quote=True)}"/><meta property="og:url" content="{canonical}"/><meta property="og:image" content="__SITE_URL__/assets/og-orbit.png"/><meta property="og:image:width" content="1200"/><meta property="og:image:height" content="630"/><meta property="og:image:alt" content="ORBIT developer command center brand card"/>
<meta name="twitter:card" content="summary_large_image"/><meta name="twitter:title" content="{escape(title,quote=True)}"/><meta name="twitter:description" content="{escape(description,quote=True)}"/><meta name="twitter:image" content="__SITE_URL__/assets/og-orbit.png"/>
<link rel="icon" type="image/svg+xml" href="/assets/favicon.svg"/><link rel="stylesheet" href="/assets/site.css"/><script src="/assets/site.js" defer></script>
<script type="application/ld+json">{structured or '{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"WebPage","name":"'+escape(title,quote=True)+'","url":"'+canonical+'"}'}</script></head>
<body>{header}<main id="main">{body}</main>{footer}</body></html>'''
    dest=root/slug.strip('/')/'index.html' if slug!='/' else root/'index.html'
    dest.parent.mkdir(parents=True,exist_ok=True)
    dest.write_text(page,encoding='utf-8')

home='''<section class="hero"><div class="container hero-grid"><div class="hero-copy"><span class="pill"><span class="dot" aria-hidden="true"></span> ORBIT · Invite-only beta</span><h1>Your dev workflow.<br/><span class="accent">One clear orbit.</span></h1><p>Bring GitHub and GitLab repositories, issues, pull requests, CI signals, and approval-gated AI tasks into one focused developer workspace.</p><div class="actions"><a class="btn primary" href="#pilot">Explore the private pilot <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a><a class="btn secondary" href="#workflow">How ORBIT works <span aria-hidden="true">↓</span></a></div><div class="trust"><span>Read-only repo browsing</span><span>MFA-gated access</span><span>Developer-first workflow</span></div></div>
<div><div class="preview" aria-label="Illustrative ORBIT interface preview"><div class="app-top"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span>ORBIT / command-center</span></div><div class="app-shell"><div class="app-side"><div>◈ Overview</div><div>▤ Repositories</div><div>☷ Tickets</div><div>✳ Agent jobs</div><div>⌘ Settings</div></div><div class="app-view"><small>WORKSPACE / OVERVIEW</small><h3>Everything in focus.</h3><div class="stats"><div class="stat"><span>Repo feeds</span><b style="color:#63d8fb">02</b></div><div class="stat"><span>Review items</span><b style="color:#b6a4ff">06</b></div><div class="stat"><span>Job approvals</span><b style="color:#89f2be">01</b></div></div><div class="window"><div class="window-head">Development activity <span class="chip">Example data</span></div><div class="task"><span>⌁ GitHub · Review open PR</span><small>Review</small></div><div class="task"><span>⎇ GitLab · Check pipeline</span><small>Passing</small></div><div class="task"><span>✦ Codex task · Awaiting approval</span><small>Queued</small></div></div></div></div></div><p class="screen-caption">Illustrative interface preview; not a live customer account.</p></div></div></section>
<section class="section" id="features"><div class="container"><div class="section-head"><div class="eyebrow">Everything within reach</div><h2>Less switching. More shipping.</h2><p>A focused view of the work already happening across your development tools, without asking you to replace them.</p></div><div class="feature-grid">
<article class="feature-card"><div class="symbol" aria-hidden="true">⑂</div><h3>Repository visibility</h3><p>Browse available GitHub and GitLab projects from a single workspace. Access depends on each provider's granted permissions.</p></article>
<article class="feature-card"><div class="symbol" aria-hidden="true">☷</div><h3>Issues and code reviews</h3><p>Read issues, pull requests, merge requests, and basic CI activity without leaving your daily dashboard.</p></article>
<article class="feature-card"><div class="symbol" aria-hidden="true">✦</div><h3>Approval-gated AI jobs</h3><p>Stage AI-assisted development tasks for explicit approval. The agent worker is available only to trusted pilot operators.</p></article>
<article class="feature-card"><div class="symbol" aria-hidden="true">▦</div><h3>Personal ticket board</h3><p>Turn external issues into tracked work inside your private Kanban board, without editing upstream tickets.</p></article>
<article class="feature-card"><div class="symbol" aria-hidden="true">◎</div><h3>One focused workspace</h3><p>Keep repositories, tasks, and activity together with personal workspace persistence and account-scoped access.</p></article>
<article class="feature-card"><div class="symbol" aria-hidden="true">◇</div><h3>Control over integrations</h3><p>Connect scoped provider credentials and disconnect when needed. Commercial OAuth onboarding is on the roadmap.</p></article></div><div class="platforms" aria-label="Supported providers"><span class="platform">GitHub</span><span class="platform">GitLab</span><span class="platform">Supabase Auth</span><span class="platform">Codex (trusted operator)</span><span class="platform">Claude planning (trusted operator)</span></div></div></section>
<section class="section alt" id="workflow"><div class="container split"><div><div class="eyebrow">A simpler development loop</div><h2>From repo activity to your next action.</h2><p>ORBIT gives you the context to decide what matters before you hand off work.</p><div class="step"><span class="num">01</span><div><h3>Connect your tools</h3><p>Use a scoped, read-only GitHub or GitLab credential during the pilot.</p></div></div><div class="step"><span class="num">02</span><div><h3>See the relevant work</h3><p>Browse your accessible repos, review items, and CI signals.</p></div></div><div class="step"><span class="num">03</span><div><h3>Track and approve</h3><p>Keep tasks on your board and explicitly approve privileged agent jobs.</p></div></div></div><div class="code-card" aria-label="Example workflow"><div class="code-head"><span>ORBIT / workflow preview</span><span>READ-ONLY CONNECTORS</span></div><pre>// One workspace. Clear boundaries.

repo = connect("github", "read-only")
issues = repo.listIssues()
prs = repo.listPullRequests()

board.track(issues[0])
agentJob = planTask("Review this PR")

// Agent execution requires approval.
agentJob.requestApproval()</pre><p class="muted" style="font-size:12px;margin-bottom:0">Pseudocode illustrating product behavior, not a public SDK.</p></div></div></section>
<section class="section" id="safety"><div class="container split"><div><div class="eyebrow">Designed for deliberate access</div><h2>Read first.<br/>Act intentionally.</h2><p>Repository connections fetch data through a server function; ORBIT does not automatically push commits or merge requests.</p><a class="btn secondary" href="/security/">Read our security approach <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div><div class="security-bullets"><p>Repository data is read through provider API calls; the connector does not request write operations.</p><p>Connection credentials are designed for server-side encrypted storage, not browser local storage.</p><p>Access to private workspaces is gated by login, approval, and multi-factor authentication in the pilot.</p><p>AI agent execution is separate from ordinary account access and requires manual approval.</p></div></div></section>
<section class="section alt" id="faq"><div class="container"><div class="section-head"><div class="eyebrow">Questions</div><h2>Everything you need to know.</h2></div><div class="faq">
<details><summary>Is ORBIT available to everyone?</summary><p>Not yet. ORBIT is an invite-only beta. We are validating integrations and security before accepting general signups.</p></details>
<details><summary>Can ORBIT read my private GitHub and GitLab repositories?</summary><p>Yes, when your provider grants the necessary read permissions. During the beta, each user supplies a scoped access token for their selected account.</p></details>
<details><summary>Can ORBIT commit, merge, or deploy changes automatically?</summary><p>No. The repository connectors are read-only. Trusted operators may configure a separate approval-gated local agent worker; it is not available to ordinary pilot accounts.</p></details>
<details><summary>Does ORBIT support other tools?</summary><p>Earlier owner-only integrations include YouTrack; the V6 pilot focuses on per-user GitHub and GitLab connections. Additional integrations are planned, not promised.</p></details>
<details><summary>Is there a price?</summary><p>Public pricing has not been announced. ORBIT is currently being evaluated as an invite-only pilot.</p></details>
</div></div></section>
<section class="section" id="pilot"><div class="container"><div class="callout"><div><div class="eyebrow">ORBIT private pilot</div><h2>Better flow starts with a clearer workspace.</h2><p>We’re building a developer tool with useful integrations and careful approval controls. Want to be considered for the pilot?</p></div><a class="btn primary" href="mailto:__CONTACT_EMAIL__?subject=ORBIT%20private%20pilot">Request pilot access <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div></div></section>'''
