features='''<section class="subpage-hero"><div class="container"><div class="eyebrow">Developer integrations</div><h1>Know what’s happening across GitHub and GitLab.</h1><p>ORBIT puts read-only repository information beside the tasks you’re already tracking. During the private pilot, users connect individually scoped access tokens.</p></div></section><section class="section"><div class="container feature-grid"><article class="feature-card"><div class="symbol">⑂</div><h3>GitHub repositories</h3><p>View repositories accessible to your token and inspect issues, open pull requests, and workflow status. Organization approval may be necessary for private repos.</p></article><article class="feature-card"><div class="symbol">⎇</div><h3>GitLab projects</h3><p>Browse GitLab.com projects, open merge requests, issues, and pipelines with a scoped <code>read_api</code> token.</p></article><article class="feature-card"><div class="symbol">▦</div><h3>Personal task tracking</h3><p>Use your Kanban board to track external work. Tracking an issue does not change it in GitHub or GitLab.</p></article></div></section><section class="section alt"><div class="container split"><div><div class="eyebrow">Pilot boundaries</div><h2>Designed to see clearly, not overreach.</h2><p>ORBIT deliberately limits the repository connector to read operations and known provider API endpoints. Repository code content is not currently analyzed by these connections.</p><a class="btn secondary" href="/security/">Security details</a></div><div class="security-bullets"><p>Only GitHub.com and GitLab.com are supported in the per-user connector beta.</p><p>Token management is manual. Self-serve OAuth and refresh flows are not available yet.</p><p>Results currently use bounded first-page lists rather than exhaustive pagination.</p><p>Use fine-grained GitHub permissions or GitLab read_api for the least necessary access.</p></div></div></section><section class="section"><div class="container"><div class="callout"><div><h2>Bring your workflow into focus.</h2><p>Explore the private pilot and get in touch about early access.</p></div><a class="btn primary" href="mailto:__CONTACT_EMAIL__?subject=ORBIT%20integrations%20pilot">Ask about the pilot</a></div></div></section>'''
layout('GitHub & GitLab Repository Dashboard | ORBIT','See GitHub and GitLab repositories, issues, pull requests, merge requests, and CI activity in ORBIT’s read-only developer dashboard.','/features/',features)
security='''<section class="subpage-hero"><div class="container"><div class="eyebrow">Security and access</div><h1>Know what ORBIT can access.</h1><p>Security boundaries should be understandable. These describe the current pilot architecture, not an independent security certification.</p></div></section><div class="container prose"><h2>Authentication</h2><p>The private application uses Supabase authentication and an approved-user list. A verified second factor (MFA) is required for private workspace features.</p><h2>Read-only integrations</h2><p>GitHub and GitLab repository connections are accessed by authenticated server functions. Provider tokens are designed to be encrypted with AES-GCM before storage and are never intended for display after connection.</p><p>The connector limits upstream requests to known GitHub.com and GitLab.com APIs using GET operations. Read-only API access does not make a broader provider token harmless: choose the narrowest possible permissions and short expiry dates.</p><h2>Agent boundaries</h2><p>The V5 agent job queue is approval-gated. Execution is restricted to an explicitly authorized operator with a local worker. Customer accounts are not automatically granted code execution.</p><h2>What we have not completed</h2><ul><li>An independent penetration test or formal security certification.</li><li>Production-ready OAuth account linking and automated token rotation.</li><li>Public self-service subscriptions or enterprise account administration.</li><li>Production incident response and contractual service-level commitments.</li></ul><div class="notice">ORBIT is an invite-only pilot. Do not assume enterprise certification, compliance audits, or production SLAs.</div><h2>Questions</h2><p>To request security details, <a href="mailto:__CONTACT_EMAIL__?subject=ORBIT%20security%20question">contact the ORBIT team</a>.</p></div>'''
layout('Security & Permissions | ORBIT Developer Command Center','How ORBIT handles GitHub and GitLab read-only access, multi-factor authentication, encrypted credentials, and approval-gated agent jobs.','/security/',security)
privacy='''<section class="subpage-hero"><div class="container"><div class="eyebrow">Privacy overview</div><h1>Privacy in the ORBIT pilot.</h1><p>This page is a plain-language product privacy overview, not a complete legal privacy policy. A jurisdiction-specific policy must be published before general customer onboarding.</p></div></section><div class="container prose"><div class="notice"><strong>Pilot only:</strong> Please do not invite customers based on this overview alone. Obtain legal review and publish a complete GDPR-compliant notice before commercial launch.</div><h2>Information the product handles</h2><p>When configured, ORBIT uses Supabase to manage accounts and private workspace data. The read-only provider connector can retrieve GitHub and GitLab repository metadata, issues, pull/merge requests, and CI status using user-supplied access tokens.</p><h2>Credential handling</h2><p>Provider access tokens are transmitted to a protected server function and designed to be encrypted at rest. Access tokens should never be committed to source control or placed in browser storage. Disconnecting a provider deletes the saved encrypted token, but provider-side revocation should also be performed when appropriate.</p><h2>Third parties</h2><p>The pilot is built on Supabase and accesses provider APIs when connected. Before launch, the operator must document the applicable service providers, legal bases, retention periods, international transfers, user rights and contact details.</p><h2>Contact</h2><p>For pilot questions, <a href="mailto:__CONTACT_EMAIL__?subject=ORBIT%20privacy%20question">contact the ORBIT team</a>.</p></div>'''
layout('Privacy Overview | ORBIT Developer Command Center','An overview of what the ORBIT private pilot handles, including Supabase workspace data and GitHub/GitLab repository metadata.','/privacy/',privacy)
